Found under k314 (2026-10-31). k314 corrects the Cpanel::JSON::XS eq/ne operand swap on JSON::PP::Boolean in lib/OCP.pm, at load. That covers every process that loads OCP first: bin/ocp, and robocop via OCP::Robocop::Controller. The Rex child that runs share/Rexfile decodes REX_TASK_PARAMS with JSON::MaybeXS but never loads OCP.pm, so there `'word' eq $true` is still true for any word.

Not reachable today: only two right-hand `eq` in share/Rexfile (lines ~653 and ~896, both CIDR strings), and gpu/ntp params arrive as 0/1. It becomes a bug the moment the Rexfile compares a boolean param on the right of eq.

Done = the Rexfile process gets the same correction (load the fix from one place, not a copy, e.g. move it into a small module both load), or the Rexfile params are normalised to 0/1 before use and that is pinned by a test. Lane: ocp-infra-worker.

2026-10-31 07:42 Reproduced red in raudssus/ocp:latest (Cpanel::JSON::XS backend): a copy of share/Rexfile run as rex -f <copy> -e <probe> from a cwd outside the checkout, REX_TASK_PARAMS={"probe":true}: task_params() hands back a JSON::PP::Boolean and 'hetzner' eq it is 1. Load path checked: in the image the rex child's @INC is the local-lib only (PERL5LIB=/opt/ocp/install/perl5/lib/perl5); bin/ocp's 'use lib $FindBin::Bin/../lib' does not reach a child, and OCP::Rex runs a /tmp copy of the Rexfile, so a module in lib/ is NOT loadable there today. Under prove -l it would be: prove exports PERL5LIB=/src/lib:..., and Rex itself puts <cwd>/lib and <rexfile dir>/lib ahead of PERL5LIB (Rex::generate_inc), and make test runs from /src. So a test that just runs rex under prove would pass while the image dies; the test has to strip the checkout's lib from PERL5LIB and run from a directory outside the checkout.

